.TH XD\-BLUETOOTH 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-bluetooth \- Bluetooth Devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-bluetooth
.RB [ \-\-add | \-\-options ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-bluetooth
is Windows XP SP2's Bluetooth Devices (Control Panel), over BlueZ's D-Bus
interface:
.TP
.B Devices
The paired devices: Add (the Add Bluetooth Device Wizard), Remove and
Properties.
.TP
.B Options
Discovery, new pairings, the notification area icon, and the computer's
Bluetooth name.
.TP
.B Hardware
The Bluetooth radios.
.PP
While it runs, it is BlueZ's pairing agent, asking for passkeys and
confirmations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-add
Only the Add Bluetooth Device Wizard (the notification area icon's Add a
Bluetooth Device).
.TP
.B \-\-options
Open on the Options tab.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR xd\-control (1)
